        "original_id": "4d0b19cb-2e4f-5e1d-85a1-885722f15240",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Yorkshire Terrier, Cavalier King Charles Spaniel, Chihuahua, Papillon, Pointer\n- Organizations: The Kennel Club, American Kennel Club\n- Medical conditions: Hypoplasia of dens\n- Places: Yorkshire, England\n\nFacts:\n- The Yorkshire Terrier was developed during the 19th century in Yorkshire, England.\n- The Yorkshire Terrier is a small terrier-type dog breed that was developed to catch rats in clothing mills.\n- The Cavalier King Charles Spaniel is a small spaniel that The Kennel Club and the American Kennel Club classify as a toy dog.\n- Hypoplasia of dens is more commonly seen in the Chihuahua, the Papillon, the Pointer, and the Yorkshire Terrier.",
